Comment (internal/api/handler/workflows/import.go:74):
**Low — over-limit *chunked* uploads report 400, not the documented 413.**

The route is wrapped with Echo `BodyLimit`, but when a request has no `Content-Length` (chunked/streaming), `BodyLimit` returns `echo.ErrStatusRequestEntityTooLarge` *during* `ctx.MultipartForm()` → `ParseMultipartForm`. This handler funnels every `MultipartForm()` error into a generic 400, so the swagger-documented `413` is only ever returned for `Content-Length` overages (rejected by the middleware before the handler) or the explicit `len(files) > maxImportFiles` / per-file-size paths.

Suggestion: when `err` is an `*echo.HTTPError` (or `errors.Is(err, echo.ErrStatusRequestEntityTooLarge)`), propagate its status code instead of hard-coding 400, so over-limit bodies consistently surface as 413.
